{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Give police emergency powers to return children withheld by a parent",
        "additional_details": "Currently, when a parent breaks a family court order and refuses to return a child, the police often refuse to intervene, calling it a \"civil matter\". Parents are forced to wait months for new court hearings while their children are alienated and legal orders are ignored with impunity. The law has a dangerous gap. We need emergency police enforcement powers to protect children and uphold court decisions immediately, instead of allowing parents to break the law while waiting for future court.",
        "background": "We call on the Government to amend the law to grant police immediate emergency powers to recover a child when a parent withholds them in breach of an active Court Order or shared care agreement.",
